    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d585-a1">

                <pb facs="0693" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg607"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Prinetti to Mr.
                            Meyer.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1903-01-01"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 1,
                    1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I hasten to thank your
                    excellency for the notes of December 29 and 1st instant, and I beg you to convey
                    to his excellency, the President of the United States, the sentiments of
                    gratitude of the Government of the King, for his good offices which were
                    inspired by extreme courtesy.</p>
                <p>As I already had the honor of communicating to your excellency, the Government of
                    the King has no difficulty, in principle, to refer its claims to the arbitration
                    of The Hague.</p>
                <p>To reply to the other points indicated in the notes above mentioned, the
                    Government of the King has already hastened to place itself in communication
                    with the cabinets of London and Berlin.</p>
                <p>Pray accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Prinetti.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
